from pathlib import Path
import numpy as np,json
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
O=Path(__file__).parent;j=json.loads((O/'rigging-offset-comparison.json').read_text());a=np.load(O/'rigging-shared_offsets.npz');b=np.load(O/'rigging-per_flight_offsets.npz')
f,axs=plt.subplots(1,3,figsize=(13,4))
for ax,i in zip(axs,[0,5,6]):
 ax.plot(a['t'],np.rad2deg(a['truth'][i]),color='black',lw=2,label='Recorded bank');ax.plot(a['t'],np.rad2deg(a['model'][i]),label='Shared offsets');ax.plot(b['t'],np.rad2deg(b['model'][i]),label='Offsets by flight');day,start=j['validation_windows'][i];ax.set(title=f'{day}, {start} s',xlabel='Forecast time (s)',ylabel='Payload bank (deg)');ax.grid(alpha=.2)
axs[0].legend(fontsize=8);f.suptitle('Rigging offsets alone do not resolve the turn mismatch');f.tight_layout();f.savefig(O/'iteration-rigging-offsets.png',dpi=160)
p=O/'physics-development.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s=s.replace('</html>','''<section id="rigging-offsets"><h2>Testing the confirmed rigging adjustment</h2><p>The pilot confirms a rigging adjustment; its timing, side and magnitude remain unspecified. A diagnostic fit therefore allows separate effective left/right engagement offsets for Hood River and Trout Lake while retaining shared bank dynamics and the exact logged PWM-to-drum-travel mapping. This is a hypothesis about configuration, not evidence of when the adjustment occurred.</p><figure><img src="iteration-rigging-offsets.png" alt="Recorded bank compared with shared and flight-specific brake-offset fits"><figcaption>Three-second bank-only forecasts with causal initial-rate estimates and actuator history. These previously inspected turns are development checks, not sealed final tests.</figcaption></figure><p>Three-block chronological cross-validation within each flight worsens from 6.17 to 6.99 degrees RMS when offsets vary by flight. Some early Trout Lake turns improve, but the late high-bank case worsens. Estimated offsets vary markedly between folds, so they cannot be interpreted as measured rigging changes. The model holds inferred initial airspeed constant and does not yet represent full coupled flight dynamics. Result: retain the confirmed rigging change as configuration uncertainty, but reject separate offsets as a sufficient fix.</p><p>Reproduction: <code>fit_rigging_offsets.py</code>; parameters, split definitions and errors: <code>rigging-offset-comparison.json</code>. The five quarantined Trout Lake blocks remain unused.</p></section></html>''');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
